{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1576087400,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MzY1MzA2ODY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3920","origin":"github"},"title":"remove does not commit removal of subdatset","message":"As reported in #3919, `remove` does not commit the removal of a subdataset on either master or 0.11.x.  That is inconsistent with how `remove` behaves with non-dataset items (unless `--nosave` is given).\n\n`remove` still uses annotated paths, so perhaps the most feasible fix is to just couple this with the rewrite to drop annotated paths from `remove`.  With 0.12.x, we've talked about moving away from most subcommands saving things themselves, and requiring a follow-up call to `save`, so going that direction would of course resolve this issue as well.","files":null}]}